{"name":"Incense Cedar","hex":"#65644a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"incense cedar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the species of coniferous trees of the genus Calocedrus, with fragrant wood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incense_cedar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calocedrus","blocks":[{"text":"Calocedrus, the incense cedar, is a genus of coniferous trees in the cypress family, Cupressaceae, first described as a genus in 1873. Three species are native to eastern Asia and one to western North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Calocedrus_decurrens_7947.jpg/330px-Calocedrus_decurrens_7947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calocedrus","wikidata":"Q765246"},{"title":"Incense","blocks":[{"text":"Incense is an aromatic biotic material that releases fragrant smoke when burnt. The term is used for either the material or the aroma. Incense is used for aesthetic reasons, religious worship, aromatherapy, meditation, and ceremonial reasons. It may also be used as a simple deodorant or insect repellent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/R%C3%B6kelse_SSB_Helga_Trefaldighet_gif.gif/330px-R%C3%B6kelse_SSB_Helga_Trefaldighet_gif.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incense","wikidata":"Q273131"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Incense_Cedar_in_Lassen_VNP.jpg/500px-Incense_Cedar_in_Lassen_VNP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Incense_Cedar_in_Lassen_VNP.jpg/500px-Incense_Cedar_in_Lassen_VNP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"California incense cedar, in Lassen Volcanic National Park","link":"https:/